    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\ntrailspace\n\n### Description\n\nWhen I run `MiniTrailspace.trim()` in my config, the LSP complains that `MiniTrailspace` is an unknown global variable.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to be able to do `require('mini.trailspace').trim()` instead.\r\n\r\nHmmmm.... so I just tried it, and I can! Awesome!\r\n\r\nSo now my feature request is to mention this in the docs.",
